{"step_index":99,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:19:34Z","content":"All approved resolutions have been posted to the comment threads in the Google Doc:\n\n🔗 **[HR Agentic Solution BRD - Reviewed & Annotated](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MwYH70ssudg0-_SjPjZQndfjtsD0ca616YYNB0NgS5g/edit)**\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Comment Thread Status & Resolutions Added\n\n| # | Section & Comment Topic | User Action / Alignment | Final In-Line Resolution Added to Doc |\n| :---: | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1** | **Sec 6:** Auth & Credentials Conflict | Approved Option B | `[Resolution]: Adopt Gateway Mock Identity Assertion (Signed JWT Header) for MVP 1. The Chat UI injects authenticated user claims ('employee_id', 'role', 'department') into request headers. This enables end-to-end RBAC and audit origin verification without requiring full production SSO/Okta integration.` |\n| **2** | **NFR-4.3:** Orchestration Consistency | Approved Forward Escalation | `[Resolution]: Adopt Forward Escalation with DLQ. For partial failures across chained actions, the system will: (1) not rollback successful HCM state, (2) push a high-priority event to an HR Ops Dead-Letter Queue, and (3) notify the user with a specific partial-success summary and reference ID.` |\n| **3** | **NFR-2.1:** Latency Targets | Approved p50/p95 SLAs | `[Resolution]: Update Latency SLAs: (1) Policy Q&A RAG: p50 < 1.5s, p95 < 3.0s; (2) Single-system transactions: p50 < 2.0s, p95 < 4.0s; (3) Cross-system orchestration: p50 < 4.0s, p95 < 7.0s with streaming UI progress indicators.` |\n| **4** | **FR-5.5:** Document Sync Latency SLA | Approved $\\le 1\\text{h}$ SLA | `[Resolution]: Set sync SLA to <= 1 hour for automated webhook/change-data-capture ingestion, with a manual 'Sync Now' admin trigger and a daily scheduled full re-indexing batch (24 hours).` |\n| **5** | **FR-4.3:** Duplicate Ticket Mitigation | Approved 15m Window | `[Resolution]: Define deduplication parameters: (1) Time window = 15 minutes; (2) Matching heuristic = Same caller ID + same category + cosine similarity > 0.85 on short description; (3) Behavior = Prompt user: 'A similar ticket [ID] was recently created. Do you want to view it or add a comment instead?'` |\n| **6** | **FR-4.2:** Ticket Lifecycle Permissions | Approved User Role Bounds | `[Resolution]: Restrict end-user conversational permissions to: (1) Query details, (2) Create incident, (3) Post comment, (4) Cancel ticket (if state = New). Updating state to 'Resolved' or 'Closed' is restricted to fulfiller roles.` |\n| **7** | **FR-3.4:** Real-time Fetch & Resilience | Approved Circuit Breaker | `[Resolution]: Implement a 5-second timeout with exponential backoff (max 2 retries) and a circuit breaker. If WorkWeek is unavailable, degrade gracefully by informing the user that real-time balance queries are temporarily offline while keeping Policy Q&A active.` |\n| **8** | **FR-3.2:** Leave Scope & Approvals | Approved Approval Workflow | `[Resolution]: For MVP 1: (1) Leave requests default to 'Submitted for Manager Approval' state; (2) Business calendar logic excludes weekend days and designated company holidays from work-day calculations; (3) Leave Cancellation and Modification are added to Should-Have (MVP 1.1).` |\n| **9** | **FR-1.5:** RBAC & Data Isolation | Approved Orchestration RBAC | `[Resolution]: RBAC will be enforced at the Agent Orchestration layer using the signed gateway user context. The agent will strictly filter data access using caller 'employee_id', preventing prompt-based cross-user data exposure.` |\n| **10** | **UC-2.3:** Building Access Boundary | Approved Out of Scope | `[Resolution]: Closed as Out of Scope. Per decision on Comment #14, UC-2.3 (Relocation & Facilities Badge Access) is deferred from MVP 1.` |\n| **11** | **Sec 3 (UC-2.2):** SAGA Consistency | `action:discuss it` | `[Agreed Resolution]: Adopted Forward Escalation with DLQ. WorkWeek leave is retained; ServiceImmediately ticket failure triggers an alert to the HR Operations dead-letter queue with a transparent partial-success reference provided to the user.` |\n| **12** | **Sec 3 (UC-2.1):** Autonomous Ordering | `action:accept the change` | User confirmed: Requires explicit confirmation card before ordering hardware. |\n| **13** | **Sec 3 (UC-1.2):** PTO Units | `action:change hrs to days` | User confirmed: Standardized to work days. |\n| **14** | **Sec 2.3:** Scope Contradiction (UC-2.3) | `action:consider out of scope` | User confirmed: UC-2.3 (Relocation) marked out of scope. |\n| **15** | **Sec 1:** Zero Policy Violations | `action:accept the change` | User confirmed: Converted to probabilistic safety metrics ($>99.5\\%$). |\n| **16** | **Sec 1:** 40% Deflection Metric | `action: take assumptions` | `[Agreed Resolution]: Baseline assumed at 5,000 Tier-1 inquiries/month (60% IT, 40% HR). Deflection defined as resolved self-service or policy Q&A with positive feedback/no ticket within 24h. Target: 2,000 tickets/month (40%) by Month 6.` |\n| **17** | **Exec Summary:** Zero-Trust vs. SSO | `action:discuss various options` | `[Agreed Resolution]: Adopted Option B (Gateway Mock Identity Assertion with Signed JWT Header) for MVP 1. Enables zero-trust RBAC simulation and audit logging without requiring full enterprise Okta/SSO integration.` |\n\n---\n\n### Ready for Next Steps\nAll 17 discussion threads and action items are now closed with clear engineering specifications. If you would like to apply these changes directly to the body text of the document or generate updated architecture diagrams, let me know!"}
