{"step_index":111,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:21:04Z","content":"The revised, production-ready version of the Business Requirements Document has been created and formatted with standard typography and structure:\n\n🔗 **[HR Agentic Solution BRD (MVP 1 - Revised & Approved)](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gW-lwRWN1sltc0jUolYhFktNlzJ3App5d7z4AkivZlI/edit)**\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Major Architectural & Requirements Fixes Incorporated\n\n| Section in New BRD | Key Revisions & Fixes Incorporated |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Executive Summary** | • **Identity Architecture:** Defined the **Gateway Mock Identity Assertion Layer** (signed JWT session claims passed via `X-Authenticated-User`) to reconcile zero-trust origin authentication with test-credential sandboxes.<br>• **Safety Standards:** Updated from deterministic \"zero violation\" claims to calibrated probabilistic benchmarks ($\\ge 99.5\\%$). |\n| **Section 1: Project Objectives** | • **40% Deflection Baseline:** Grounded against an enterprise baseline of **5,000 Tier-1 inquiries/month** (60% IT, 40% HR), with a defined target of deflecting $\\ge 2,000$ inquiries/month by Month 6.<br>• **Deflection Attribution:** Explicitly defined as resolved self-service or policy Q&A with positive feedback and no ticket opened within 24 hours. |\n| **Section 2: Project Scope** | • **Scope Governance:** Formally marked **UC-2.3 (Relocation & Facilities Badging)**, payroll processing, and multi-lingual translation as **Out of Scope for MVP 1** (deferred to Phase 2). |\n| **Section 3: Use Cases** | • **UC-1.2 (Leave Balances):** Standardized all balance metrics and prompt examples strictly to **work days**.<br>• **UC-2.1 (Procurement):** Added mandatory **Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) Confirmation Cards** before creating procurement orders.<br>• **UC-2.2 (Medical Leave):** Formalized **Forward Escalation with Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ)** to handle partial failure gracefully without data corruption. |\n| **Section 4.1 & 4.2: Security & Dialog** | • **RBAC & Isolation (FR-1.5):** Enforced at the Agent Orchestration layer using signed Gateway claims to prevent prompt-based cross-user data leakage.<br>• **Context Lifecycle (FR-2.2):** Defined a 30-minute inactivity timeout and explicit `/reset` session purging. |\n| **Section 4.3: WorkWeek Integration** | • **Leave State (FR-3.2):** Submissions default to `Submitted for Manager Approval`.<br>• **Calendar Rules (FR-3.3):** Excludes weekends and company holidays from requested durations.<br>• **Resilience (FR-3.4):** Configured real-time fetch with a 5-second timeout, 2 exponential backoff retries, and circuit-breaker degradation messaging. |\n| **Section 4.4: ServiceImmediately** | • **Role Permissions (FR-4.2):** Restricts end-users to querying, creating, commenting, and canceling (`New` state only). Status transitions to `Resolved`/`Closed` are restricted to fulfillers.<br>• **Deduplication (FR-4.3):** Defined concrete heuristics (15-minute window, same caller, category match, cosine similarity $> 0.85$ prompting user). |\n| **Section 4.5: Policy RAG** | • **Sync SLA (FR-5.5):** Specified $\\le 1\\text{ hour}$ webhook/CDC sync SLA, supported by an admin manual sync endpoint and 24-hour batch refresh. |\n| **Section 5: Non-Functional Requirements** | • **Latency SLAs (NFR-2.1):** Set concrete targets: Policy RAG $p50 < 1.5\\text{s}, p95 < 3.0\\text{s}$; Single-system transactions $p50 < 2.0\\text{s}, p95 < 4.0\\text{s}$; Chained orchestration $p50 < 4.0\\text{s}, p95 < 7.0\\text{s}$.<br>• **SAGA & Resilience (NFR-4.3):** Standardized on `Idempotency-Key` headers and Forward DLQ escalation. |\n| **Section 6: Implementation Architecture** | • **Clear Architectural Boundaries:** Formalized the separation between the Chat UI persona selector, Gateway JWT assertion, and backend sandbox service accounts. |"}
