{"step_index":142,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:25:26Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-17T14:25:26Z\nCompleted At: 2026-08-17T14:25:31Z\n\n\t\t\t\tThe command exited with code 0.\n\t\t\t\tOutput:\n\t\t\t\tUse Case ID --- Category --- Triggering User Prompt (Example) --- Systems Involved --- System Actions / Expected Behavior\r\nUC-1.1 --- Policy Q&A --- \"What is the company's bereavement leave policy?\" or \"Are employees allowed to expense noise-canceling headphones?\" --- Policy Docs --- Query policy documents, retrieve relevant sections, and present a grounded answer with citation metadata (URLs/Deep Links).\r\nUC-1.2 --- HR Self-Service --- \"How many days of PTO do I currently have accrued?How many hours of PTO do I currently have accrued?\" or \"Please submit a time-off request for this coming Thursday and Friday.\" --- WorkWeek (HCM) --- Retrieve current leave balances in work days; validate business calendar (excluding holidays/weekends); render confirmation card; submit time-off request in 'Submitted for Approval' state in WorkWeek.Retrieve current leave balances or validate and submit a time-off request in WorkWeek.\r\nUC-1.3 --- IT Incident Mgmt --- \"What is the status of ticket INC123456?\" or \"Create an IT ticket because my VPN connection keeps dropping.\" --- ServiceImmediately (ITSM) --- Query status/comments or create a new support incident ticket in ServiceImmediately.\r\nUC-2.1 --- Cross-System: Equipment Procurement --- \"I just read the remote work policy and saw I'm eligible for a home office monitor. Can you verify my remote status and order one for me?\" --- Policy Docs, WorkWeek, ServiceImmediately --- 1. Query remote work policy.\r\n2. Verify user's location/status in WorkWeek.\r\n\r\n3. Generate a hardware request in ServiceImmediately with shipping details.\r\nUC-2.2 --- Cross-System: Medical Leave --- \"I need to take short-term medical leave starting next Monday. What is the process, and can you set it up for me?\" --- Policy Docs, WorkWeek, ServiceImmediately --- 1. Quote leave procedure from policy documents.\r\n2. Submit Leave of Absence in WorkWeek.\r\n3. Open ticket in ServiceImmediately to route user email access to manager.\r\nUC-2.3 --- Cross-System: Relocation --- \"I'm transferring to the London office next month. Can you tell me the relocation allowance, update my record, and get my building access sorted?\" --- Policy Docs, WorkWeek, ServiceImmediately --- 1. Quote relocation limits from policy documents.\r\n2. Prompt address update in WorkWeek.\r\n3. Open facilities badge ticket in ServiceImmediately.\r\n\n"}
{"step_index":143,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:25:32Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Use Cases**\n\nI'm currently focused on dissecting the provided text, particularly the use cases. I've noted two specific examples: generating a hardware request and opening a ticket for email access routing. Now I'm delving into UC-2.3 to identify the next component.\n\n\n**Refining Edits for Clarity**\n\nI've just finished preparing a batch of edits for the use cases and related sections. I've focused on clarity, like how UC-2.1 will require a confirmation card before generating a hardware request. I also improved UC-2.2 to include a resilience measure for failed ticket creation. UC-2.3 has been deferred to Phase 2, and the FR-1.5 has been simplified as well. Now I am going to make sure the format is right, and then add it to the tables!\n\n\n**Implementing Security Measures**\n\nI've just added strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) at the Agent Orchestration layer with verified Gateway identity claims (JWT). This will prevent unauthorized cross-user data access and exposure. I've also added a summary confirmation card before executing state-mutating transactions to satisfy FR-2.3. The WorkWeek API now uses Gateway signed JWT assertion via X-Authenticated-User for authentication. I'm also ensuring leave requests respect business calendars.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"BypassSandbox":true,"CommandLine":"/google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"Generate a hardware request in ServiceImmediately with shipping details.\" \"Render Confirmation Card with item specs and shipping address.\n4. Upon user confirmation, generate a hardware request in ServiceImmediately.\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y && /google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"Open ticket in ServiceImmediately to route user email access to manager.\" \"Open ticket in ServiceImmediately to route user email access to manager. (Resilience: If ticket creation fails, retain WorkWeek leave, emit an alert to the HR Ops DLQ, and provide user with the WorkWeek confirmation reference ID).\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y && /google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"I'm transferring to the London office next month. Can you tell me the relocation allowance, update my record, and get my building access sorted?\" \"[Deferred to Phase 2]\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y && /google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"The system must enforce strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) to ensure that users can only access their own data or authorized information, preventing unauthorized cross-user data access.\" \"The system must enforce strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) at the Agent Orchestration layer using verified Gateway identity claims (signed JWT). Ensure users can only access their own profile and ticket records, preventing prompt-based cross-user data exposure.\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y","Cwd":"/google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Suggesting changes for UC-2.x and RBAC","toolSummary":"Suggest edits for Use Cases and RBAC"}}]}
